            <ArticleTitle>Exercise at menopause: a critical difference.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Even at menopause, fitness can reduce the risk of heart disease, osteoporosis, and diabetes, yet only 38% of women over age 19 exercise regularly. A sports medicine expert recommends that exercise be encouraged and prescribed, even for women with a variety of comorbidities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
